\pxi-2.6,l2.6;1. FOR THE LOCATION OF THE PIER WALL, SEE SHEET B4-10 (PLAN AND ELEVATION). SECTIONS H-H AND J-J ARE LOCATED IN THE PIER WALL ELEVATION; FOR SECTION J-J AND THE ANNULAR RING PLATE DETAILS, SEE SHEET B4-15; FOR SECTION H-H, SEE SHEET B4-
  3
16.\P2. PIER WALL REINFORCEMENT: #5 BARS AT 11" MAXIMUM EACH WAY ON EACH FACE (5G1 VERTICALS, 5G2 HORIZONTALS), 3" CLEAR COVER; 5G3 END U RETURNS AT EACH HORIZONTAL WITH 2'-3" CONTACT LAP LEGS ALONG THE FACES; 4~5G1 VERTICALS IN EACH END FACE. THE HO
  3
RIZONTALS ARE THE OUTER LAYER.\P3. REINFORCEMENT IS SHOWN REPRESENTATIVELY: THE FIRST AND LAST BAR OF EACH RUN ARE DRAWN.\P4. ANNULAR RING PLATES: 20 PLATES, ½" THICK, 23" O.D. x 20ƃ" I.D., 5 PER PILE WITH THE PLATE TOPS 6", 3'-6", 6'-6", 9'-6", 12'-
  3
6" ABOVE THE BOTTOM OF THE WALL, CENTERED ON THE PILES AND WELDED TO THEM WITH TWO CONTINUOUS Ɖ" FILLETS (TOP AND BOTTOM OF EACH PLATE); SEE SHEET B4-15. THE PLATES ARE SHOWN HIDDEN IN THE ELEVATION.\P5. PILES ARE SHOWN AT THEIR NOMINAL LOCATIONS; TH
  3
E RING PLATES ARE SIZED FOR A 3" RADIAL PILE PLACEMENT TOLERANCE.\P6. THE CAP IS SHOWN BROKEN 1'-0" ABOVE ITS BOTTOM; FOR THE CAP, SEE SHEETS B4-10 AND B4-11.\P7. MODEL CHECK (REMOVE BEFORE ISSUE): THE SELECTED RING CALCULATION (PIER-WALL-CASE, D-084
  3
, 22 OCTOBER 2026) REPORTS THE FAILED CHECK RING-GRID (RING CLEARANCE TO INNER FACE-GRID LAYER: 1.125 IN REQUIRED, -0.75 IN AVAILABLE); RESOLVE BEFORE ISSUE.\P8. MODEL CHECK (REMOVE BEFORE ISSUE): THE PIER WALL VERTICALS STOP 3Ƅ" BELOW THE CAP AND 3Ƅ
  3
" ABOVE THE BOTTOM OF THE WALL IN THE CAD MODEL (NO ANCHORAGE INTO THE CAP); DETAIL THE WALL-TO-CAP CONNECTION AND ADD IT TO THE MODEL.\P9. MODEL CHECK (REMOVE BEFORE ISSUE): CAD MODEL STATUS OF THE PIER WALL STEEL: "CAD END U RETURN LEGS 27 IN AND R
  3
ING PLATES 1/2 IN MATCH THE SELECTED D-084 CASE (LRFD 10TH 5.10.8.2.1 DEVELOPMENT, 26-IN CLASS B LAP); WALL DIMENSIONS MATCH D-075 WITHIN 0.001 IN; RING-GRID TOLERANCE FAILURE REMAINS; ENGINEERING ACCEPTANCE OPEN".\P10. FOR REINFORCING BAR LIST, SEE 
  1
SHEET B4-21.
