\pxi-2.6,l2.6;1. FOR THE LOCATION OF SECTION J-J, SEE THE PIER WALL ELEVATION, SHEET B4-14. SECTION K-K IS LOCATED IN THE ANNULAR RING PLATE PLAN.\P2. SECTION J-J IS BROKEN BETWEEN RING ROWS 2 AND 4; THE RING PLATE TOPS ARE DIMENSIONED FROM THE BOTTO
  3
M OF THE WALL AND THE HORIZONTAL BAR SERIES IS GIVEN IN FULL.\P3. ALL BARS ARE SHOWN IN SECTION J-J; BARS IN THE SECTION PLANE ARE THE NEAREST BAR OF THEIR SERIES WITHIN 1'-3" BEYOND THE CUT. THE END U RETURNS AND THE END-FACE VERTICALS LIE BEYOND TH
  3
E CUT AND ARE NOT SHOWN; SEE SECTION H-H, SHEET B4-16.\P4. ANNULAR RING PLATES: ½" THICK, 23" O.D. x 20ƃ" I.D. (1Ɗ" RADIAL WIDTH), Fy = 50 KSI, Fu = 65 KSI; WELDED TO THE PIPE PILE WITH TWO CONTINUOUS Ɖ" FILLET WELDS, E70XX ELECTRODES, ONE AT THE TOP
  3
 AND ONE AT THE BOTTOM OF EACH PLATE. THE Ƈ" RADIAL ROOT GAP IS AN ANALYSIS ALLOWANCE; THE WPS SHALL ACCEPT IT.\P5. PIPE PILES ARE SHOWN WITH THEIR NOMINAL 20" OUTSIDE DIAMETER; THE WELD SOLIDS ARE NOT IN THE CAD MODEL.\P6. THE PLATE AND WELD SIZES A
  1
RE THOSE OF THE SELECTED PIER WALL RING CALCULATION (PIER-WALL-CASE, D-084, 22 OCTOBER 2026).\P7. FOR REINFORCING BAR LIST, SEE SHEET B4-21.
